{
  "status": "draft",
  "summary": [
    {
      "text": "Alert 5387721 concerns canonical row 5387721: a transfer of 4383.854319071021 USD on 2022-09-08 from account 216161 at bank 5 to account 252446 at bank 864, payment format \"6\", cross-bank.",
      "citations": ["transaction.amount_usd", "transaction.from_account", "transaction.to_account", "transaction.from_bank", "transaction.to_bank", "transaction.payment_format", "transaction.date", "features.is_cross_bank"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The model did not alert on this row: model.alert is false, raw_margin is -8.557985561777802 against a threshold of 0.10078280410798467, and rank_in_day is 225552 against a budget of 200.",
      "citations": ["model.alert", "model.raw_margin", "model.threshold", "model.rank_in_day", "model.budget"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The transaction is one of a repeating, near-identical set of transfers from 216161 to 252446: the same three amounts (45293.54765573514, 2983.337602005439, 4383.854319071021) recur across multiple days, and the alert row is the 4383.854319071021 leg.",
      "citations": ["get_account_history:call_00_lQAqPxbHElpHXnswELSq4651", "get_account_history:call_01_zwIAvGlPN29wOoowPqVI7405", "transaction.amount_usd"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The sender 216161 shows a pronounced fan-out: fan_out_star is true, out_degree 85 versus in_degree 12, with 85 outbound transactions to 9 distinct counterparties and 12 inbound from 3 distinct counterparties.",
      "citations": ["context.fan_star.fan_out_star", "context.fan_star.out_degree", "context.fan_star.in_degree", "context.sender_history.out.txn_count", "context.sender_history.out.distinct_counterparties", "context.sender_history.in.txn_count", "context.sender_history.in.distinct_counterparties"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The receiver 252446 is almost purely inbound: 26 inbound transactions from 4 distinct counterparties (cross_bank_frac 0.9230769230769231) against only 2 outbound transactions to 1 counterparty totalling small amounts (amount_max 491.86378289479984).",
      "citations": ["context.receiver_history.in.txn_count", "context.receiver_history.in.distinct_counterparties", "context.receiver_history.in.cross_bank_frac", "context.receiver_history.out.txn_count", "context.receiver_history.out.distinct_counterparties", "context.receiver_history.out.amount_max"]
    }
  ],
  "observed_facts": [
    {
      "text": "Alert row amount is 4383.854319071021 USD, timestamp ts_ns 1662632460000000000 (2022-09-08), from account 216161 (bank 5) to account 252446 (bank 864).",
      "citations": ["transaction.amount_usd", "transaction.ts_ns", "transaction.from_account", "transaction.to_account", "transaction.from_bank", "transaction.to_bank"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The same 4383.854319071021 USD amount from 216161 to 252446 appears in prior history at rows 4542371 (ts 2022-09-07 03:14), 3832463 (2022-09-06 01:22), 3718705 (2022-09-05 21:40), 2968942 (2022-09-04 10:01), 2587861 (2022-09-03 01:27), 2484633 (2022-09-02 22:14) and 1106628 (2022-09-01 14:39).",
      "citations": ["get_account_history:call_00_lQAqPxbHElpHXnswELSq4651", "get_account_history:call_01_zwIAvGlPN29wOoowPqVI7405"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Each of those 4383.854319071021 legs is accompanied by a 2983.337602005439 leg and a 45293.54765573514 leg from 216161 to 252446 within the same short burst (e.g. rows 4542369, 4542370, 4542371 on 2022-09-07 between 03:02 and 03:14).",
      "citations": ["get_account_history:call_00_lQAqPxbHElpHXnswELSq4651", "get_account_history:call_01_zwIAvGlPN29wOoowPqVI7405"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The sender 216161 also makes repeated small outbound payments of identical amounts to other counterparties, e.g. 1695.1545925979926 and 492.2021366157072 to 182892 (bank 751), 650.7798795441308 / 546.553181502312 / 188.33448897901056 to 216075 (bank 5), 261.74962154333326 / 187.1701981671477 to 221949 (bank 821), 1569.542169335119 / 324.3980255439727 to 265320 (bank 837).",
      "citations": ["get_account_history:call_00_lQAqPxbHElpHXnswELSq4651", "get_neighbours:call_02_SaoIs7UQl2bTcVqngDHj7444"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inbound funding to 216161 comes from account 394 (bank 22) in repeated identical amounts of 19060.098507772247 USD: rows 4808748 (2022-09-07 13:04), 3912035 (2022-09-06 04:13), 3426399 (2022-09-05 10:31).",
      "citations": ["context.subgraph.inbound_to_sender[0].amount_usd", "context.subgraph.inbound_to_sender[0].row", "context.subgraph.inbound_to_sender[1].amount_usd", "context.subgraph.inbound_to_sender[1].row", "get_account_history:call_00_lQAqPxbHElpHXnswELSq4651"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Account 394 also issues repeated identical large outbound amounts to account 233539 (bank 6390): 801063.7215105534, 307675.2149028325, 75801.30920774413 and 27831.536389399975 each appear twice (rows 4941714/4389441, 4941717/4389444, 4941716/4389443, 4941715/4389442).",
      "citations": ["get_account_history:call_00_KoZnPbByoeZGscg7mOV34506"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Both accounts are young: from_age_days is 7 and to_age_days is 7, with first_seen_ns 1661990760000000000 for the sender and 1662042780000000000 for the receiver.",
      "citations": ["features.from_age_days", "features.to_age_days", "context.sender_history.first_seen_ns", "context.receiver_history.first_seen_ns"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The receiver 252446 has no outbound transfers recorded in the subgraph window (outbound_from_receiver is empty) and only 2 outbound transactions in its full history, both to itself (counterparty 252446) at 7.097667108032645 and 491.86378289479984 USD.",
      "citations": ["context.subgraph.outbound_from_receiver", "get_account_history:call_01_zwIAvGlPN29wOoowPqVI7405", "context.receiver_history.out.txn_count"]
    },
    {
      "text": "No directed cycles were found through account 216161 (n_matching 0), and the package records cycles as empty.",
      "citations": ["find_cycles:call_01_VpRtv3CuytYgbiqLIa1P7470", "context.cycles"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The golden label for this row is 0 and features.is_laundering is 0.",
      "citations": ["transaction.golden_label", "features.is_laundering"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Bank 864 shows 2923 transactions, 1795 inbound and 889 outbound, across 166 distinct accounts and 159 counterparty banks, with bank 5 as a top counterparty (71 transactions, 2492354.47 USD).",
      "citations": ["get_bank_stats:call_00_d0PgfDSMWUFcJ11CPFAG3140"]
    }
  ],
  "hypothesised_typology": [
    {
      "text": "Hypothesis: repeated, exactly-repeating amount triplets pushed from a young, high-fan-out sender (216161) into a near-pure-receiver account (252446) are consistent with layering / pass-through placement, where value is fragmented into fixed denominations and routed through an intermediary account.",
      "citations": ["get_account_history:call_00_lQAqPxbHElpHXnswELSq4651", "context.fan_star.fan_out_star", "context.receiver_history.in.txn_count", "features.from_age_days", "features.to_age_days"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The upstream leg from 394 to 216161 in identical 19060.098507772247 USD amounts, and 394's own repeated identical large payments to 233539, suggest a multi-tier structure rather than an isolated pair of accounts.",
      "citations": ["context.subgraph.inbound_to_sender[0].amount_usd", "get_account_history:call_00_KoZnPbByoeZGscg7mOV34506"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The corpus defines structuring narrowly as breaking down currency transactions to evade CTR reporting requirements, which is the closest retrieved reference concept; it does not by itself establish a typology for this wire-only pattern.",
      "citations": ["ref:sar-faqs-october-2025:002"]
    }
  ],
  "supporting_evidence": [
    {
      "text": "Exact repetition of the same three amounts (45293.54765573514, 2983.337602005439, 4383.854319071021) across at least seven separate bursts from 216161 to 252446 is a strong indicator of scripted or templated payment behaviour rather than organic commerce.",
      "citations": ["get_account_history:call_00_lQAqPxbHElpHXnswELSq4651", "get_account_history:call_01_zwIAvGlPN29wOoowPqVI7405"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sender fan-out is structurally extreme: out_degree 85 against in_degree 12, fan_out_star true, and from_fan 10.0 with from_fan_out 6.0.",
      "citations": ["context.fan_star.out_degree", "context.fan_star.in_degree", "context.fan_star.fan_out_star", "features.from_fan", "features.from_fan_out"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The receiver's inbound is overwhelmingly cross-bank (cross_bank_frac 0.9230769230769231) while its outbound is entirely intra-bank (cross_bank_frac 0.0), consistent with funds being consolidated at 252446 rather than redeployed.",
      "citations": ["context.receiver_history.in.cross_bank_frac", "context.receiver_history.out.cross_bank_frac"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Both accounts were first seen within days of the alert (from_age_days 7, to_age_days 7), so the entire observed relationship is recent.",
      "citations": ["features.from_age_days", "features.to_age_days", "context.sender_history.first_seen_ns", "context.receiver_history.first_seen_ns"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The sender's minimum inter-transaction gap is 60 seconds (from_min_gap_seconds 60), indicating tightly clustered bursts.",
      "citations": ["features.from_min_gap_seconds"]
    }
  ],
  "counter_evidence": [
    {
      "text": "The model did not alert on this row (model.alert false, raw_margin -8.557985561777802, rank_in_day 225552 of budget 200), so the alerting signal is weak and the case rests on pattern inspection rather than model score.",
      "citations": ["model.alert", "model.raw_margin", "model.rank_in_day", "model.budget"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The golden label is 0 and features.is_laundering is 0, which is counter-evidence to the laundering hypothesis.",
      "citations": ["transaction.golden_label", "features.is_laundering"]
    },
    {
      "text": "No directed cycles exist through 216161, so a circular-flow / round-tripping typology is not supported by the data.",
      "citations": ["find_cycles:call_01_VpRtv3CuytYgbiqLIa1P7470", "context.cycles"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The retrieved corpus passages do not define a typology matching this wire-only repeated-amount pattern; the structuring definition retrieved is specific to currency transactions and CTR evasion, so the typology label is an inference, not a corpus-supported match.",
      "citations": ["ref:sar-faqs-october-2025:002", "ref:explanatory-note-for-revised-r-16:020"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The receiver's two outbound transactions are to itself (counterparty 252446), which may indicate internal transfers or data artefacts rather than genuine disbursement; this weakens any claim about where funds ultimately go.",
      "citations": ["get_account_history:call_01_zwIAvGlPN29wOoowPqVI7405"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The provenance records that original amount and currency are not carried through to the canonical table, so the USD figures may not reflect the original instructed amounts.",
      "citations": ["provenance.known_gaps[0]"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The sender history retrieval was truncated (truncated true, n_matching 92), so the full counterparty set and any additional repeated-amount patterns beyond the 40 rows returned are unverified.",
      "citations": ["get_account_history:call_00_lQAqPxbHElpHXnswELSq4651"]
    },
    {
      "text": "No SHAP drivers are stored, so the feature contributions behind the model output cannot be inspected directly.",
      "citations": ["provenance.known_gaps[1]"]
    }
  ],
  "recommended_next_steps": [
    {
      "text": "Pull the full untruncated history for account 216161 (92 matching rows) and for account 394 (116 matching rows) to confirm whether the repeated-amount pattern extends further and to enumerate all counterparties.",
      "citations": ["get_account_history:call_00_lQAqPxbHElpHXnswELSq4651", "get_account_history:call_00_KoZnPbByoeZGscg7mOV34506"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Obtain KYC and beneficial-ownership records for accounts 216161, 252446 and 394, including the 7-day account ages recorded in features.",
      "citations": ["features.from_age_days", "features.to_age_days"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Establish the business rationale for the fixed triplet of 45293.54765573514, 2983.337602005439 and 4383.854319071021 USD payments, and for the repeated 19060.098507772247 USD inbound from 394.",
      "citations": ["get_account_history:call_00_lQAqPxbHElpHXnswELSq4651", "context.subgraph.inbound_to_sender[0].amount_usd"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Clarify the nature of the receiver's two self-directed outbound transactions (7.097667108032645 and 491.86378289479984 USD) and determine where funds received by 252446 are ultimately disbursed.",
      "citations": ["get_account_history:call_01_zwIAvGlPN29wOoowPqVI7405"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Review account 394's repeated identical payments to 233539 (801063.7215105534, 307675.2149028325, 75801.30920774413, 27831.536389399975 USD) to assess whether a broader multi-tier structure exists.",
      "citations": ["get_account_history:call_00_KoZnPbByoeZGscg7mOV34506"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A human investigator should decide whether the weak model signal (rank_in_day 225552 of budget 200) and the golden label of 0 warrant continued review or closure; this draft takes no such action.",
      "citations": ["model.rank_in_day", "model.budget", "transaction.golden_label"]
    }
  ],
